WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.949
Lab 1 dry-runs the five deploy
scripts against the kits' fixtures,

3
00:00:04.949 --> 00:00:07.863
in the drift-pipeline
folder of the examples.

4
00:00:07.863 --> 00:00:10.300
Nothing signs in and nothing is called.

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.818
Step one starts clean, with no out folder,

6
00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:16.175
because the evidence records
are numbered within it.

7
00:00:16.175 --> 00:00:19.111
Step two runs the test
stage's pre-flight check,

8
00:00:19.111 --> 00:00:22.125
with the production
settings as the other file.

9
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:26.632
P F oh one to P F ten pass: the
settings schema, no secret in the file,

10
00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:31.918
no placeholder left, the cloud,
certificate paths outside the repository,

11
00:00:31.918 --> 00:00:36.772
all nine kits present, and test and
production on different tenants,

12
00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:39.025
subscriptions and identities.

13
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:41.587
The test stage needs no promotion record.

14
00:00:41.587 --> 00:00:47.386
The live probes, the Azure CLI's cloud,
tenant, subscription and signed-in identity,

15
00:00:47.386 --> 00:00:51.887
the PowerShell modules and the
certificate files, print as DRY.

16
00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:54.974
The last two lines:
zero failed, a dry run,

17
00:00:54.974 --> 00:00:58.700
and the first evidence
record, preflight pass.
